# Pipeline validation

- Run `python scripts/validate-workflow-guardrails.py` after pipeline changes.
- Run manifest and schedule schema validation after config/schema changes.
- Run `actionlint` after workflow changes and `shellcheck` after shell changes.
- Validation must fail on errors; do not downgrade lint failures to warnings.
- Every workflow must declare explicit top-level `permissions`.
- Prefer the minimum permission set and elevate only in the job that needs it.
- New scheduled manifest names must resolve to an existing manifest file.
- New external checkouts must use a separate `path`.
- Tests for guardrails must include both a passing and a failing fixture or
  exercise the failure condition against a temporary copy.
- Keep CI checks deterministic: use pinned tool/action versions and avoid
  downloading an unversioned `latest` release.
